==Quick Walkthrough==
# Spend three dragon souls to learn the words of [[Skyrim:Durnehviir (dragon)|Durnehviir]]'s shout.
# [[Skyrim:Summon Durnehviir|Summon Durnehviir]] three times while outside of the [[Skyrim:Soul Cairn|Soul Cairn]] in order to learn [[Skyrim:Soul Tear|Soul Tear]].

==Detailed Walkthrough==
[[File:SR-creature-Durnehviir 02.jpg|right|thumb|Durnehviir proclaims you Qahnaarin]]
After defeating him in the [[SR:Boneyard|Boneyard]], [[Skyrim:Durnehviir (dragon)|Durnehviir]] will rematerialize outside, hailing you as his {{hover|Vanquisher|Qahnaarin}}. He will express his surprise and admiration of your fighting ability, stating that he has never been felled on the fields of the [[Skyrim:Soul Cairn|Soul Cairn]] before. He will then recount the tale of how he came to be bound into the service of the [[Lore:Ideal Masters|Ideal Masters]], explaining that he was deceived after he sought their power to help establish his dominance among his fellow dovah on [[Lore:Nirn|Nirn]]. He will then teach you how to summon him back into Tamriel, promising to reward you each time you set him free.

Each time you do so, he will teach you another word of [[Skyrim:Soul Tear|Soul Tear]], a powerful [[Skyrim:Shouts|shout]] that deals a large amount of damage and doubles as a [[Skyrim:Soul Trap (effect)|Soul Trap]] and [[Skyrim:Reanimate Corpse|Reanimate Corpse]] spell. Moreover, after being summoned Durnehviir will also explain the meaning of each of those words. The first time he will be very glad to breathe Nirn's air once more: ''"Ah! The free air of {{hover|Nirn|Vus}} at long last. As promised, I now teach you the first word of Soul Tearing: "{{hover|Essence|Rii}}" - the essence of your enemy's life force."'' As you summon him for the second time, he explains yet another word: ''"I can feel my strength returning each time I am set free from that prison! Hear now the second word of Soul Tearing: "{{hover|Tear|Vaaz}}" - meaning to tear your enemy's soul from its living vessel."'' Unlike the Ideal Masters, this Dragon even after all the years of imprisonment, holds on to his honor and teaches you the third and final word of the Soul Tear shout, just as he promised: ''"You have kept your side of the bargain, now let me fulfill mine. Feel the last word of Soul Tearing within yourself: "{{hover|Zombie|Zol}}" - the unlife that results when a soul is imprisoned in dead flesh."'' Each word will require a Dragon Soul to learn, as if it had been learned from a [[Skyrim:Word Wall|word wall]].

==Notes==
* You will need to activate all three words of the Summon Durnehviir shout in order to call him, which will require three Dragon Souls.
* Unlike the [[Skyrim:Call Dragon|Call Dragon]] shout, the Summon Durnehviir shout works like a Conjuration spell. You have to aim it at the ground and have enough space around the point of summoning for the shout to succeed. This also means that you can summon him within certain enclosed areas such as caves as long as there is enough room.

==Bugs==
{{Bug|You can learn the shout without being able to summon Durnehviir. This can happen if the game gives you all three words at once, and you leave for Tamriel without speaking to Durnehviir again before exiting the Soul Cairn.|confirmed=1|dlc=DG}}
**{{Pc22}} Use the console command <code>player.placeatme xx00C71A</code>. Kill the dragon that spawns, either using the console or otherwise. This will have to be done multiple times to get all the quests.  You can also use console commands 'disable' and 'markfordelete' on each dragon.
{{Bug|It is not necessary to summon Durnehviir to Tamriel. Summoning him in the Soul Cairn will have the same results and dialogue.|UDGP|1.1.4|dlc=DG}}
{{Bug|It is possible to kill Durnehviir when he appears a second time before he gets a chance to speak. The quest will then never initiate.|confirmed=1|dlc=DG}}
**You can reset the quest and then set stage it to 30.
{{Bug|It's possible that Durnehviir will disappear (be banished) shortly after summoning him, even not being able to finish his sentence regarding the Thu'um he is teaching. This, however won't prevent the acquisition of the word.|confirmed=1|dlc=DG}}
**A possible solution seems to be pressing action (Activate; PC: "E") key pointing at Durnehviir while in the close proximity right after summoning him, as if one would like to interact with him. It will be entitled "<player_name>'s Durnehviir", similar to how any other summoned creatures are described.
**The partial solution is to quick save before summoning him and try - if he vanishes quick load and try summoning him some place else, even if it's only a few steps away.
{{Bug|As Summon Durnehviir shout works like a Conjuration spell, it is subject to the same bugs (see [[Skyrim:Conjuration#Bugs|Conjuration bugs]]). If you have a high [[Skyrim:Spell Absorption|Spell Absorption]] level (from the [[Skyrim:The Atronach Stone|Atronach Stone]] and Atronach [[Skyrim:Alteration#Skill Perks|Alteration perk]]), the shout will fail most of the time. One simple solution is to activate another stone, while learning the shout.}}

